# Deny everything, then name what the build actually reads.
#
# The allow-list is the safe direction here rather than a matter of taste:
# `models/` is 43 GB and `target/` is another 8, and an exclude-list that
# forgets one of them does not fail - it silently ships the context to the
# daemon on every build.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!crates

# `crates/*/static/` is read by `include_str!` at compile time and has to be
# here; nothing else under `crates/` is optional either, so the tree goes in
# whole and only build artefacts are taken back out.
crates/**/target
